hadiths[166]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2133","Asim bin 'Ubaidullah said:' I heard Salim bin 'Abdullah narrating a Hadith from his father who said: ""'Umar said : ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you see that what we do is a new matter- or a matter initiated – or it is a matter already concluded?” He (s.a.w) said: “ O Ibn Al-Khattab! It is a matter already concluded. For everyone is suited (for that for which he is created). As for one who is among the people of happiness"
"2134","""Al-'Ajwah is from Paradise and it contains a cure for poison. Truffles are a form of manna, and its liquid is a cure for the eye."""
"2135","Abdullah bin Mas'ud said:The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) narrated to us - and he is the truthful and entrusted one: 'Indeed the creation of one of you is gathered inside his mother in forty days. Then"
"2136","""Truffles are the earth's smallpox."" So the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said: ""Truffles are a form of manna, and its liquid is a cure for the eye. Al-'Ajwah is from Paradise, and it contains a cure for poison."""
"2137","""It was narrated to me that Abu Hurairah said: 'I took three truffles, or five, or seven, and pressed them. Then I put their liquid in a bottle, and I used it on the eyes of a slave girl of mine so she was cured.'"""
"2138","""It was narrated to me that Abu Hurairah  said:'Ash-Shuniz is a cure for  every disease except As-Sam.'  Qatadah said: ""One takes twenty-one seeds daily, and puts them in a cloth, then infuses (water) and sniffs two drops in his right nostril, and one drop in the left. The second (day) two drops are sniffed in the left, and one drop in the right. The third (day) two drops in the right and one drop in the left."""
"2139","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) came out to us with two books in hand. And he said: 'Do you know what these two books are?' We said: 'No"
"2140","""I entered upon 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim Abu Mabad Al-Juhani to visit him, while he had Humrah. I said:'Why don't you hang something?' He said: 'Death is better than that. The Prophet (S.A.W) said: ""Whoever hangs something, he is entrusted to it.""

Another chain reports a similar narration."
"2141","Ibn Mas'ud narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) stood among us and said: 'One thing does not infect another.' So a Bedouin said: 'O Messenger of Allah! If a camel gets mangy glands and we leave it at the resting place of camels"
"2142","Jabir bin 'Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'A slave (of Allah) shall not believe until he believes in Al-Qadar"
"2143","""For fever, and all pains, the Prophet (S.A.W) would teach them to say: Bismillahil-Kabir; a'udhu billahil-'Azimi min sharri kulli 'irqin na'arin, wa min sharri harrin-nar. (In the name of Allah the Great, I seek refuge with Allah the Magnificent from the evil of every gushing vein, and from the evil of the heat of the Fire)"""
"2144","Matar bin 'Ukamis narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""When Allah decrees that a slave (of His) is to die in a land"
"2145","Abu 'Azzah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""When Allah decrees that a slave (of His) is to die in a land"
"2146","# Scholarly Translation of the Hadith

**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatādah, from Abū ʿAbdullāh, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allāh be pleased with him), that the Prophet ﷺ used to prescribe olive oil and wars¹ for the treatment of *dhāt al-janb* (pleurisy).**

**Qatādah said:** ""And he would apply it to the side from which the patient was suffering.""

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. And Abū ʿAbdullāh's name is Maymūn; he is a Basran shaykh.""

---

**Notes:**

1. **Wars** (الورس): A plant known as *Memecylon tinctorium* or a type of safflower-like dye plant, traditionally used in folk medicine for its therapeutic properties.

2. **Dhāt al-janb** (ذات الجنب): A classical Arabic medical term referring to pleurisy or a painful inflammatory condition of the thoracic region.

3. **Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ**: A grading terminology used by Imām al-Tirmidhī (may Allāh have mercy on him) indicating that the hadith possesses both *ḥasan* (good) and *ṣaḥīḥ* (authentic) qualities, reflecting the strength of its chain of narration."
"2147","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""There are two groups in my Ummah for whom there is no share in Islam: The Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah."" Another chain reports a similar narration"
"2148","""The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) came to me while I had a pain that almost ruined me. So,the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said: 'Rub it with your right hand seven times and say A`udhu bi `Izzatillah Wa Qudratihi wa Sultanihi min sharri ma ajid."" (""I seek refuge in Allah's might, power, an authority, from the evil of what I suffer.)"" He said: ""So I did it, and Allah removed what I had, and I never ceased telling my family and others to do it."""
"2149","""Shubrum"" He said: ""It is hot and too strong."" She said:""Then I used Senna as a laxative."" So the Prophet (S.A.W) said: ""If there was anything that would have a cure for death in it, then it would have been Senna."""
"2150","""A man came to the Prophet (S.A.W) and said: 'My brother is suffering from loose bowels.' He said: 'Let him drink Honey.' So he drank it. Then he came and said: O Messenger of Allah (S.A.W)! He has drunk honey, but it has only made him more worse.' So the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said: ' Let him drink honey.'"" He said: ""So he drank it. Then he came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah (S.A.W)! I gave him some more to drink, but it has only made him more worse.'"" He said: ""The Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said: 'Allah has told the truth,and your brother's stomach has lied. Give him honey to drink'. So he gave him some more honey to drink and he was cured.'"""
"2151","""There is no Muslim worshiper who visits one who is ill - other than at the time of death - and he says seven times: As'alullah Al-'Azeem Rabbal 'Arshil 'Azeem an yashfik ('I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne to cure you') except when he will be cured."""
"2152","""When one of you suffers from fever - and indeed fever is a piece of the Fire - let him extinguish it with water. Let him stand in a flowing river facing the direction of it and say: Allahummashfi 'abdaka wa saddik Rasulak ('In the name off Allah. O Allah! Cure your slave and testify to Your Messenger.)' Doing so after Salat As-Subh(Fajr) and before the rising of the sun. Let him submerse himself in it three times, for three days. If he is not cured in three, then five. If he is not cured in five, then seven. If he is not cured in seven, then nine. For indeed it will not remain after nine, with the permission of Allah."""
"2153","Abdul-Wahid bin Sulaim narrated:""I arrived in Makkah and met 'Ata bin Abi Rabah. I said to him: 'O Abu Muhammad! The people of Al-Basrah speak about Al-Qadar.' He said: 'O my son! Do you recite the Quran?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then recite Az-Zukhruf to me.'"" He said: 'So I recited: Ha Mim. By the manifest Book. Verily"
"2154","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Allah decreed the measures fifty-thousand years before He created the Heavens and the earth"
"2155","'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: 'Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Sakuni narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you visit a sick person, give him hope for a long life, for that will not change anything, but it will comfort his soul."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a gharib hadith."
"2156","Hannad and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Abu Salih al-Ash'ari, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) visited a man suffering from a fever and said: ""Good news! For Allah says: 'It is My fire, which I inflict upon My sinful servant so that it may be his portion of the Fire (in this world, thus reducing his punishment in the Hereafter).'""

Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan (al-Basri), who said: They used to hope for a night of fever as an expiation for sins that had been committed.

The Book of Medicine is complete. It is followed by the Book of Inheritance (al-Fara'id)."
"2157","Abu Hurairah said:""Idolaters from the Quraish came to the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) quarreling about Al-Qadar. So this Ayah was revealed: ""The day they will be dragged on their faces into the Fire (it will be said to them): ""Taste you the touch of Hell."" Verily we have created all things with Qadar"
"2158","""Learn the laws of inheritance and the Quran, and teach the people, for I am a mortal."""
"2159","""The wife of Sa'd bin Ar-Rabi came with her two daughters from Sa'd to he Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)and said; O Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)! these two are daughters of Sa'd bin Ar-Rabi who fought along with you on the day of Uhud and was martyred. Their uncle took their wealth, without leaving any wealth for them, and they will not be married unless they have wealth.' He said: 'Allah will decide on that matter.' The ayah about inheritance was revealed, so the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) sent  (word) to their Uncle saying: Give the two daughters of Sa'd two thirds, and give their mother one eighth, and whatever remains, then it is for you.'"
"2160","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah, who said:** Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, who said:

A man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabi'ah and asked them about the share of the daughter, the daughter of the son, and the full sister. They said: ""The daughter receives one-half, and the full sister receives the remainder."" They then said to him: ""Go to 'Abdullah and ask him, for he will concur with us.""

So he went to 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him, and informed him of what they had said. 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Then I would be astray, and I would not be among the guided. Rather, I shall judge between them as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged: the daughter receives one-half, the daughter of the son receives one-sixth — completing the two-thirds — and the full sister receives the remainder.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **This is a hasan hadith.**

And Abu Qays al-Awdi's name is 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan al-Kufi. Shu'bah also narrated this hadith from Abu Qays."
"2161","""You recite this ayah: After payment of legacies he(or she) may have bequeathed or debts, without causing harm. And indeed the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged the debt before the will and that the children  (sons and daughters)from the same mother and father inherit,not the sons from various mothers. The man inherits from his brother from his father, and his mother, not his brother from his father.

Another chain reports a similar narration."
"2162","""The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged that the children (sons and daughters) from the same mother and father inherit, not the sons from various mothers."""
"2163","""The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) came to visit me while I was ill at Banu Salamah. I said : 'O  Prophet of Allah(S.A.W)! How shall I divide my wealth among my children?' But he did not say anything to me, until the following was revealed: Allah commands you regarding  your children's (inheritance): to the male, a portion equal to that of two females."""
"2164","""I was ill, so the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)came to visit me and found me unconscious. He came walking while Abu Bakr and 'Umar were with him. The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) performed Wudu, then poured the remaining water on me, so I came to my senses. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah(S.A.W)! how shall I dispose of my wealth?' - or - 'What shall I do with my wealth?' He did not reply anything to me"" -and he had nine sisters- ""until the Ayah about the inheritance was revealed: they ask you for a legal verdict. Say: ""Allah directs (thus) about Al-Kalalah."" Jabir said: ""It was revealed regarding me."""
"2165","Ibn 'Umar narrated:"" 'Umar delivered a Khutbah to us at Al-Jabiyah. He said: 'O you people! Indeed I have stood among you as the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) stood among us"
"2166","""A man came to the Prophet (S.A.W) and said"" 'My son died, so what do I inherit from him?' He said: 'For you is a sixth.' When he turned to leave,he called him and said: 'For you is another sixth.' So when he turned to leave , he called him saying: 'The last sixth is consumable for you.'"""
"2167","""A grandmother - the mother of a mother, or the mother of a father - came to Abu Bakr and she said: 'a son of my son' - or, 'a son of my daughter died, and I have been informed that there is a right ( from the wealth) for me in the Book.' So Abu Bakr said: 'I do not find that there is a right for you in the Book, and I have not heard that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged anything for you. I shall ask the people.' So, Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah testified that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) gave her (case) a sixth. He said: 'And who heard that along with you?' He said: 'Muhammad bin Maslamah.'"" He said: ""So he gave her a sixth. Then the other grandmother who was left behind came to 'Umar."" Sufyan said: ""And  Ma'mar said to me in addition, from Az-Zuhri - and I do not remember it to be from Az-Zuhri, rather I remember it to be from Ma'mar - that 'Umar said: 'If the two of you are together then it is for both of you, and whichever of you is alone with it (the sixth), then it is for her.'"""
"2168","""A grandmother came to Abu Bakr to ask him about her inheritance. He said to her, 'There is noting for you in the Book of Allah and there is nothing for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W). So ,return until I ask the people. So he asked the people and  Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah said: 'I was  present when the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) gave her (case) a sixth.' So he said: 'Was anyone else with you?' Muhammad bin Maslamah stood to say the same as what  Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah said. So Abu Bakr implemented that for her."" Then the other grandmother came to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab to ask him about her inheritance. He said: 'There is nothing in the Book of Allah for you, but there is that sixth. So if the two of you are together then it is for both of you, and whichever of you remains), then it is for her.'"""
"2169","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Either you command good and forbid evil"
"2170","""'Umar bin Al-Khattab sent me with a letter to Abu'Ubaidah (saying) that The Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said : 'Allah and His Messenger are responsible for the one who has no patron. And the maternal uncle inherits from the one who has no heirs.'"""
"2171","Umm Salamah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) mentioned the army that the earth would swallow"
"2172","Tariq bin Shihab said:""The first to advance the Khutbah before the Salat was Marwan. A man stood to say to Marwan: 'You have contradicted the Sunnah.' So he said: 'O so-and-so! What was there it has been left.' So Abu Sa'eed said: 'As for this"
"2173","An-Nu'man bin Bashir narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""The parable of the one who upholds Allah's laws and the one who breaches them"
"2174","Sa'id bin 'Abdur-Rahman Al-Makhzumi and more than one other narrator narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri. (Another chain:) And 'Ali bin Hujr narrated to us, [saying]: Hushaim informed us, from Az-Zuhri, from 'Ali bin Husain, from 'Amr bin 'Uthman, from Usamah bin Zaid, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim."" Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us, [saying]: Sufyan narrated to us, [saying]: Az-Zuhri narrated to us similarly.

Abu 'Eisa said: There is something on this topic from Jabir and 'Abdullah bin 'Amr. This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. It has been narrated in this manner by Ma'mar and more than one other narrator, from Az-Zuhri, similar to this. Malik narrated from Az-Zuhri, from 'Ali bin Husain, from 'Umar bin 'Uthman, from Usamah bin Zaid, from the Prophet (ﷺ), similarly. The Hadith of Malik is a mistake; Malik erred in it. Some of them narrated it from Malik saying ""from 'Amr bin 'Uthman,"" and most of the companions of Malik said ""from Malik, from 'Umar bin 'Uthman."" 'Amr bin 'Uthman bin 'Affan is well known among the children of 'Uthman, while 'Umar bin 'Uthman is not known. The practice is upon this Hadith according to the people of knowledge. Some of the people of knowledge differed regarding the inheritance of the apostate; most of the people of knowledge among the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others granted the wealth to his Muslim heirs. Others said that his Muslim heirs do not inherit from him, and they used as evidence the Hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ): ""A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever."" This is the view of Ash-Shafi'i."
"2175","Abdullah bin Khabbab bin Al-Aratt narrated from his father:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) performed Salat"
"2176","Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Indeed Allah gathered the earth for me so that I saw its east and its west. And surely my Ummah's authority shall reach over all that was shown to me of it. And I have been granted the two treasures; the red and the white. I asked my Lord that my Ummah is not to be destroyed by a universal drought"
"2177","""'Umar said: 'The blood-money is upon the 'Aqilah, and the wife does not inherit anything from the blood-money of her husband.' So Ad-Dahhak bin Sufyan Al-Kilabi informed him that the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) wrote to him, (saying) to give the wife of Ashyam Ad-Dababi the inheritance from her husband's blood-money.'"""
"2178","the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged the payment of a Gurrah male or female slave in the case of a woman's fetus from Banu Libyan which miscarried. Then the woman who was required to give the Gurrah died, so the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) judged that her inheritance be given to her children and her husband, and that her blood-money be paid by her 'Asabah."
"2179","'I asked the  Messenger of Allah(S.A.W): What is the Sunnah regarding a man among the people of the Shirk who accepts Islam at the hand of a man among the Muslims?' So the Messenger of Allah(S.A.W) said:
""He is the closet of the people to him in his life and in his death.'"""
"2180","Abu Waqid Al-Laithi narrated that when the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) went out to Hunain he passed a tree that the idolaters called Dhat Anwat upon which they hung their weapons. They(the Companions) said:""O Messenger of Allah! Make a Dhat Anwat for us as they have a Dhat Anwat.' The Prophet (s.a.w) said: ""Subhan Allah! This is like what Musa's people said: Make for us a god like their gods. By the One in Whose is my soul! You shall follow the way of those who were before you"
"2181","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The Hour will not be established until predators speak to people and until the tip of a man's whip and the straps on his sandal speak to him"
"2182","""The woman collects three inheritance: Whomever she freed, whomever she found, and the child for which she made Li'an."""
"2183","Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas narrated: I fell ill during the year of the Conquest with an illness that brought me close to death. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to visit me, and I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I have a great deal of wealth and no one will inherit from me except my daughter. Shall I bequeath all of my wealth?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Then two-thirds of my wealth?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Then half?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Then a third?"" He said: ""A third, and a third is a lot. It is better for you to leave your heirs wealthy than to leave them poor, begging from people. Whatever you spend seeking thereby [the reward of Allah], you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel of food that you lift to your wife's mouth."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my emigration [i.e., die in Mecca]?"" He said: ""You will not be left behind after me to do a deed by which you seek the Face of Allah, but that you will increase thereby in rank and standing. Perhaps you will be left long enough that some people will benefit through you and others will be harmed through you. O Allah, complete for my companions their emigration, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd bin Khawlah"" - the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) lamented for him because he died in Mecca.

[Abu 'Eisa said:] There is also a narration on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas. This is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. This hadith has been narrated through more than one route from Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. The people of knowledge act upon this, that a man may not bequeath more than a third [of his wealth]. Some of the people of knowledge held it desirable to give less than a third, due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): ""And a third is a lot."""
"2184","""Indeed a man, and a woman, perform deeds in obedience to Allah for sixty years, then death presents itself to them, and they cause such harm in the will that the Fire becomes warranted for them.""Then he recited: After payment of legacies he (or she) may have bequeathed or debts, without causing harm. This is a Commandment from Allah. up to His saying: That is the magnificent success."
"2185","Aishah narrated ""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:'In the end of this Ummah there will be a collapse"
"2186","# Hadith Ṣaḥīḥ

**Narrated by Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif:**

He said: ""I asked Ibn Abī Awfā (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) make a bequest?' He replied, 'No.' I asked, 'Then how was the bequest written, and how did he command the people?' He answered, 'He bequeathed the Book of Allah.'""

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīh gharīb* hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Mālik ibn Mighwal.

---

*Note: This narration is recorded by al-Tirmidhī in his Sunan, in the chapters on the explanation of the obligation of the Book of Allah. The chain of transmission passes through Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ → Abū Qaṭan ʿAmr ibn al-Haytham al-Baghdādī → Mālik ibn Mighwal → Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif → ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu).*"
"2187","""During the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, I heard the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) saying in the Khutbah: 'Indeed Allah, Most Blessed and Most High, has given the right due to everyone deserving a right. So there is no will for an heir, the child is for the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone, and their reckoning is for Allah, Most High. And whoever claims someone other than his father, or an affiliation with other than his Mawali, then upon him is the continued curse of Allah until the Day of Judgment. The wife is not to spend from her husband's house except with her husband's permission.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Not even food?' He said: 'That is the most virtuous of our wealth.' And he said: 'The borrowed is to be returned, the endowment is to be refunded and the debt is to be repaid, and the guarantor is responsible.'"""
"2188","""The Prophet (s.a.w) gave a Khutbah upon his she-camel, while I was under the front of her neck, and she was chewing her curd, with her saliva dripping between my shoulders. I heard him saying: 'Indeed Allah, Most Blessed and Most High, has given the right due to everyone deserving a right. So there is no will for an heir, the child is for the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone.'"""
"2189","Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Harith, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that the debt takes precedence over the bequest, whereas you recite the bequest before the debt. Abu 'Isa said: The practice according to the generality of the scholars is that the debt is given priority over the bequest."
"2190","**Narrated by Abu Habibah al-Ta'i:**

My brother bequeathed part of his estate to me. I met Abu al-Darda' and said, ""My brother has bequeathed a portion of his wealth to me. Where do you advise me to distribute it—among the poor, the needy, or those striving in the Cause of Allah?"" He replied, ""As for me, if I were in your place, I would not overlook those striving in the Cause of Allah. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: *'The one who manumits a slave at the time of death is like the one who gives charity only when he is satiated.'*""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a *hasan sahih* hadith."
"2191","# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, that 'A'ishah رضي الله عنها informed him that Barirah came seeking the assistance of 'A'ishah رضي الله Regarding the payment of her manumission contract, and she had not yet paid anything of her contract. So 'A'ishah رضي الله عنها said to her: ""Return to your family, for if they wish that I pay your manumission contract on your behalf and that your clientage (al-wala') be mine, I shall do so.""**

**Barirah mentioned that to her family, but they refused and said: ""If she wishes to seek reward on your behalf, let her do so, but the clientage (al-wala') shall be ours.""**

**She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""Purchase her and set her free, for indeed the clientage (al-wala') belongs to the one who sets free.""**

**Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said: ""What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah, it is not valid for him, even if he stipulates it a hundred times.""**

**Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. It has been narrated through other chains from 'A'ishah رضي الله"
"2192","""The Wala' is for the one who gives the price, or for the one who grants the favor.""

 There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Umar and Abu Hurairah.
This Hadith is Hasan Sahih, and this is acted upon according to the people of knowledge."
"2193","the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited selling the Wala' and  conferring it.


 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. We do not know of it except as a narration of 'Abdullah bin Dinar from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ). Shu'bah, Sufyan Ath-Thawri, and Malik bin Anas (also) reported it from 'Abdullah bin Dinar. It has been related that Shu'bah said: ""I so wished that 'Abdullah bin Dinar would permit me when he narrated this Hadith that I stand-up, so that I kiss his head."" And Yahya bin Sulaim reported this Hadith from 'Ubaidullah bin 'Umar from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ). But this is mistaken, Yahya bin Sulaim erred in it, what is correct is: ""From 'Ubaidullah bin 'Umar, from 'Abdullah bin Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ). This is how it is reported by more than one narrator from 'Ubaidullah bin 'Umar.



 And 'Abdullah bin Dinar is alone with this Hadith."
"2194","""'Ali delivered a Khutbah for us in which he said: 'Whoever claims that we have some book to read other than Allah's Book and this paper, which include camel's ages and things related to (relatiation for) wounds, then he has lied."" And he said in it: ""Al-Madinah is sacred, what is between 'Air to Thawr, so whoever introduces in it any innovation or shelters an innovator then upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. On the Day of Judgment, Allah will not accept his compulsory nor optional good deeds. And whoever claims someone else to be his father, or claims Wala' for someone other than his Mawali, then upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and the people; his compulsory and optional good deeds shall not be accepted. The covenants of the Muslims are one, it covers the rest of them.

 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Some of them reported it similarly from Al-A'mash, from Ibrahim At-Taimi, from Al-Harith bin Suwaid from 'Ali.


."
"2195","""that a man from "" He said: 'Yes."" He said: ""Then what are their colors?"" He said: ""Red."" He said: ""Is there a gray one among them?"" He said: ""Yes, there is a grey one among them."" He said: ""From where does that come?"" He said: ""Perhaps it is hereditary."" He said: ""Then in the same way, perhaps it is his heredity."" 


 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih."
"2196","""Don't you see that the Mujazziz looked just now at Zaid bin Harithah and Usamah bin Zaid, and said: 'These feet belong to each other.'""


 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih."
"2197","""Dont you see that the Mujazziz passed by Zaid bin Harithah and Usamah bin Zaid while their heads were covered, and their feet were exposed, and he said: 'These feet belong to each other.'""
This is how Sa'eed bin Abdur-Rahman - and more than one narrator - narrated this Hadith from Sufyan bin 'Uyanah, from Az-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from A'ishah. And this Hadith is Hasan Sahih. 
Some of the people of knowledge used this Hadith to support the case of Qa'if."
"2198","""Give gifts, for indeed the gift removes bad feelings from the chest. And let the neighbor not look down upon (the gift of) her neighbor, even if it be the lower shanks of sheep."" 


 This Hadith is Gharib from this route. Abu Ma'shar's name is Najih, the freed slave of Banu Hisham. Some of the people of knowledge criticized him due to his poor memory."
"2199","Ahmad bin Mani' narrated to us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq narrated to us, Husain Al-Muktib narrated to us, from 'Amr bin Shu'aib, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

""The example of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that eats until it is full, then vomits, then returns and eats its vomit.""

Abu 'Eisa said: And in this chapter there is also a narration from Ibn 'Abbas and 'Abdullah bin 'Amr."
"2200","""It is not lawful for a man to give a gift and then take it back, except in the case of the father with what he gave to his son. And the parable of the one who gives a gift, and then takes it back, is that of a dog who eats until he is full, and vomits, then he returns to his vomit."" 


 This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Ash-Shafi'i said: ""It is not lawful for one who confers something to take it back, except in the case of the father. He may take back what he gave his son"" and he used this Hadith as proof."
"2201","""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) came out to us while we were discussing about Al-Qadar. He became angry such that his face became red, as if a pomegranate  was bursting through his cheeks. He said: 'Is this what I ordered you to do?' - or: 'Is this what I have been sent to you with? The people before you were only ruined when they differed about this matter. I order you  to not debate about it.'"". (Daif))"
"2202","""Adam and Musa argued, Musa said: ""O Adam! You are the one that Allah created with His Hand, and blew into you of His Spirit, and you misled the people  and caused them  to be expelled from Paradise.'  So Adam said: 'You are Musa, the one Allah selected with His Speech! Are you blaming me for something I did which Allah had decreed for me, before creating the heavens and the earth?'"" He said: "" So Adam confuted Musa."""
"2203","' I heard Salim bin 'Abdullah narrating a Hadith from his father who said: ""'Umar said :
""O Messenger of Allah! Do you see that what we do is a new matter- or a matter initiated – or it is a matter already concluded?” He (s.a.w)  said: “ O Ibn Al-Khattab! It is a matter already concluded. For everyone is suited (for that for which he is created). As for one who is among the people of happiness, then he works for happiness, and as for the one who is among the people of misery, then he works for his misery.” (Hasan)"
"2204","Narrated by al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr and Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

""While we were with the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him), he was striking the ground (with a stick), when he raised his head toward the sky and said: 'There is not one among you except that his seat in the Fire and his seat in Paradise have already been known.' Wakīʿ said: '...except that his seat in the Fire and his seat in Paradise have already been written.' They said: 'Shall we not then rely (upon this decree), O Messenger of Allāh?' He said: 'No, work, for each one is facilitated for that for which he was created.'""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."
"2205","The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) narrated to us - and he is the truthful and entrusted one:
'Indeed the creation of one of you is gathered inside his mother in forty days. Then, for a similar period, he is a clot. Then, for a similar period, he is a piece of flesh. Then Allah sends the angel to him to blow the soul into him, and he is ordered to write four (things): To write his provision, his life-span, his works, and whether he will be wretched or happy. By the One besides Whom there is none other worthy of worship! One of you will do deeds of the people of Paradise, until there is between him and it but a forearm span, then he is overcome by what is written for him, and he is sealed off with the deeds of the people of the Fire, so that he enters it. And indeed one of you will do deeds of the people of the Fire, until there is between him and it but a forearm span, then he is overcome by what is written for him, and he is sealed off with the deeds of the people of Paradise, so that he enters it.'""

Another chain reports a similar narration."
"2206","""Every child is born upon the Millah, then his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or an idolater."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about those  who die before that?"" He said: ""Allah knows best what they would have done.""

[Another chain) with similar in 
meaning, and he said: ""Born 
upon the Fiirah."""
"2207","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour will not be established until 'Allah"
"2208","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:"" The earth will throw out pieces of its liver(in sides): liver; gold and silver will come out like columns."" He said: ""A thief will come and say: 'For this my hands were amputated?' A murderer will come and say: 'For this I killed?' One who severed ties of kinship will come and say: 'For this I severed the ties of kinship?' Then they will leave it without taking anything from it"
"2209","""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) came out to us with two books in hand. And he said:
'Do you know what these two books are?' We said: 'No, O Messenger of Allah ! Unless you inform us.' He said about the one that was in his right hand: 'This is a book from the Lord of the worlds, in it are the names of the people of Paradise, and the name of their fathers and their tribes. Then there is a summary at the end of them, there being no addition to them nor deduction from them forever.' Then he said about the one that was in his left: 'This is a book from the Lord of the worlds, in it are the names of the people of Fire, and the name of their fathers and their tribes. Then there is a summary at the end of them, there being no addition to them nor deduction from them forever.' The companions said: 'So why work O Messenger of Allah! Since the matter is already decided (and over)?' He said: 'Seek to do what is right and draw nearer, for indeed the inhabitant of Paradise, shall have his work sealed off with the deeds of the people of Paradise, whichever deeds he did. And indeed the inhabitant of Fire, shall have his work sealed off with the deeds of the people of Fire, whichever deeds he did.' Then the Messenger of Allah motioned with his hands, casting them down and said: 'Your Lord finished with the slaves, a group in Paradise, and a group in the Blazing Fire.'""

Another chain reports a similar narration."
"2210","""When  Allah wants good for a slave, He puts him in action."" It was said: ""How does he put him in action O Messenger Of Allah?"" He said: ""By making him meet up with the righteous deeds before death."""
"2211","""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) stood among us and said:
'One thing does not infect another.' So a Bedouin said: 'O Messenger of Allah! If a camel gets mangy glands and we leave it at the resting place of camels, then all of the camels get mange?' The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'Who caused the first to get mange? There is no 'Adwa nor safar. Allah created every soul, so he wrote its life, its provision, and its afflictions.'""

Note: The majority of scholars interpret this to mean that these things in and of themselves do not transmit or cause harm through supernatural or hidden means but that Allah is ultimately in control and any fearful superstition around these is false."
"2212","'A slave  (of Allah) shall not believe until he believes in Al-Qadar, its good and its bad, such that he knows that what struck him would not have missed him, and that what missed him would not have struck him."""
"2213","'A slave (of Allah) shall not believe until he believes in four: The testimony of La Ilaha Illallah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah whom He sent with the Truth, and he believes in the death, and he believes in the Resurrection after death, and he believes in Al-Qadar.""

Another chain reports a similar narration."
"2214","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour and I were dispatched like these two"" - and Abu Dawud(a narrator) indicated with his index and middle fingers- so"
"2215","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""The Hour shall not be established until you fight a people whose sandals are made out of hair"
"2216","""O Messenger of Allah! Do you think that the Ruqyah we use, the treatments we use, and what we seek to protect ourselves with prevent anything from Allah's Decree?' He said: 'They are from Allah's Decree.'"""
"2217","# Translation of the Hadith

**Wāṣil ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Kūfī narrated to us, saying:** Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us, from al-Qāsim ibn Ḥabīb and ʿAlī ibn Nizār, from Nizār, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:

**The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:**

*""Two groups from my Ummah shall have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.""*

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿUmar, Ibn ʿUmar, and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj. This is a gharīb, ḥasan, ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""**

**Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us, saying:** Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Salām ibn Abī ʿAmrah narrated to us, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him.

Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ said: **""And Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, saying:** ʿAlī ibn Nizār informed us, from Nizār, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, **a similar narration.""**

---

*Note: The Murji'ah (المرجئة) are those who deferred judgment on major sinners, and the Qadariyyah ("
"2218","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour shall not be established until nearly thirty imposters"
"2219","'From (the signs of) the son of Adam's prosperity, is his satisfaction with what Allah decreed for him, and from the son of Adam's misery is his avoiding to request guidance from Allah, and from the son of Adam's misery is his anger with what Allah decreed for him."""
"2220","""So-and-so conveys his Salam to you."" So he said: ""It has been conveyed to me that he has innovated, so if he has indeed innovated, then do not convey my Salam to him, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) saying: 'In this Ummah' or: 'In my Ummah'"" - the doubt was his - ""a collapse of the earth, or a transformation, or stones shall rain upon the people of Al-Qadr.'"""
"2221","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The best of people are my generation"
"2222",""" Six are cursed, being cursed by Allah and by every Prophet that came: The one who adds to Allah's Book, the one who denies Allah's Qadar, the one who rules with tyranny by which he honors whom Allah has debased, and he dishonors whom Allah has honored, and the one who legalizes what Allah forbade, and the one from my family who legalizes what Allah forbade, and the abandoner of my Sunnah."""
"2223","""I arrived in Makkah and met 'Ata bin Abi Rabah. I said to him: 'O Abu Muhammad! The people of Al-Basrah speak about Al-Qadar.' He said: 'O my son! Do you recite the Quran?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then recite Az-Zukhruf to me.'"" He said: 'So I recited: Ha Mim. By the manifest Book. Verily, We have  made it a Qur'an in Arabic that you may be able to understand. And verily, it is in the Mother of Book with Us, indeed exalted, full of wisdom. Then he said: 'Do you know what Mother of Books is?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know better.' He said:'It is a book that Allah wrote before He created the Heavens, and before  He created the earth. In it, it is  (written): Fir'awn is among the inhabitants of the Fire, and in it is: Perish the two hands of Abu Lahab, and perish he!'Ata said: 'I met Al-Walid the son of 'Ubadah bin As-Samit the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) and asked him:'What was your father's admonition when he died?"" He said:""He called me and said: 'O my son ! Have Taqwa of Allah, and know that you will never have Taqwa of Allah until you believe in Allah, and you believe in Al-Qadar- all of it-its good and its bad. If you die upon other than  this you shall  enter  the Fire. Indeed  I heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w)  saying: ""Verily the first of what Allah created was the Pen. So He said: 'Write.' It said : 'What shall I write?' He said : 'Write Al-Qadar, what it is , and what shall be, until  the end.'"""
"2224","Ziyad bin Kusaib Al-'Adawi said:""I was with Abu Bakrah under the Minbar of Ibn 'Amir while he was giving a Khutbah wearing a fine garment. Abu Bilal said: 'Look at our Amir wearing clothes of wickedness!' So Abu Bakrah said: Be quiet! I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying: ""Whoever insults Allah's Sultan on the earth"
"2225","""Idolaters from the Quraish came to the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) quarreling about Al-Qadar. So this Ayah was revealed:
""The day they will be dragged on their faces into the Fire (it will be said to them): ""Taste you the touch of Hell."" Verily we have created all things with Qadar."
"2226","# Hadith of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (رضي الله عنه) on the Occasion of the Day of the House (Yawm al-Dār)

**Narration:**

Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, that **ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān** (رضي الله عنه), on the **Day of the House** (*Yawm al-Dār*), looked down over the wall and said:

> ""I adjure you by Allah — do you know that the **Messenger of Allah** (صلى الله عليه وسلم) said:
>
> *'The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except for one of three: adultery after marriage (*zinā baʿda iḥṣān*), apostasy after Islam (*irtidād baʿd Islām*), or the taking of a life unjustly, for which one is killed.'*

By Allah, I never committed fornication (*zinā*) in the **Jāhiliyyah** (pre-Islamic period of ignorance), nor in Islam; nor did I ever apostatize since I pledged allegiance to the **Messenger of Allah** (صلى الله عليه وسلم); nor did I ever take the life which Allah has forbidden. **So on what basis are you killing me?**""

---

**Commentary of Imām Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (رحمه الله):**

Abū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: ""There are narrations on this topic from **Ibn Masʿūd** (رضي الله عنه), **ʿĀʾishah** (رضي الله عنها), and **Ibn ʿAbbās** (رضي الله عنهما).""

He further stated: **""This is a ḥasan (good) hadith.""**

He also noted: **Ḥammād ibn Salamah** narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and **raised it** (*rafʿahu*, i.e., attributed it to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم). However, **Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān** and others narrated this same hadith from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd but **stopped it** (*awqafūhu*) at the level of the Companion's statement and did not raise it.

He concluded: ""This hadith has been narrated through **multiple chains** from ʿUthmān (رضي الله عنه) from the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) as a **marfūʿ** (elevated) narration.""

---

## Scholarly Notes:

- **Yawm al-Dār** refers to the tragic day in which ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (رضي الله عنه), the third Rightly Guided Caliph (*Khalīfah al-Rāshid*), was besieged in his home and ultimately martyred in 35 AH (656 CE).
- The hadith establishes the **fundamental Islamic principle** that the sanctity of Muslim blood is inviolable, and capital punishment is restricted exclusively to three categories, as established by the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم).
- ʿUthmān (رضي الله عنه) invoked this hadith as a **legal and moral defense** against the charges laid by the rebels who besieged him, demonstrating his profound knowledge of the Sunnah and his unwavering adherence to Islamic conduct throughout his life.
- The discussion of **rafʿ** (elevation to the Prophet صلى الله عليه"
"2227","""During the Farewell Pilgrimage, I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying:
'Which day is this?' They said:'The day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar.'He said:'Indeed your blood, your wealth, your honour is sacred to each other, just as this day of yours is sacred in this city of yours. Indeed, no one commits a crime except against himself. Indeed none commits a crime for which his son is accountable, nor does a child commit a crime for which his father is held accountable. Indeed Ash-Shaitan has lost hope of ever being worshipped in this city of yours, but he will have compliance in what deeds of yours you consider insignificant, which he will be content with.""'"
"2228","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The night and the day shall not go away until a man called Jahjah among the Mawali reigns"
"2229","""Yazid performed Hajj in the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Prophet (s.a.w) when I was seven years old."" So 'Ali bin Al-Madini narrated from Yahya bin Sa'eed Al-Qattan: ""Muhammad bin Yusuf was a very reliable narrator of Hadith, and As-Sa'ib bin Yazid was his grandfather, and Muhammad bin Yusuf would say: 'As-Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated to me- and he is my grandfather from my mother's side.""'"
"2230","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The world shall not pass away until a man from the people of my family rules the Arabs whose name agrees with my name"
"2231","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn Mu'āwiyah al-Jumaḥī al-Baṣrī**, who narrated from **Ḥammād ibn Salamah**, from **Abū al-Zubayr**, from **Jābir** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

> **The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a sword be handed over while drawn (unsheathed).**

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *""In this chapter (there is also a narration) from Abū Bakrah (may Allāh be pleased with him).""*

He further said: *""This is a **ḥasan gharīb** ḥadīth from the narration of Ḥammād ibn Salamah.""*

He added: *""Ibn Lahī'ah also narrated this ḥadīth from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from Bint al-Juhniyy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). However, the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah is, in my view, more authentic (aṣaḥḥ).""*

---

### Scholarly Notes:

- **"
"2232","Zaid bin Al-'Ammi said:""I heard Abu As-Siddiq An-Naji narrate a Hadith from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri who said: 'We feared events to occur after our Prophet"
"2233",""" 'Umar delivered a Khutbah to us at Al-Jabiyah. He said: 'O you people! Indeed I have stood among you as the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) stood among us, and he said: ""I order you (to stick to) my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then lying will spread until a man will take an oath when no oath was sought from him, and a witness will testify when his testimony was not sought. Behold! A man is not alone with a woman but the third of them is Ash-Shaitan. Adhere to the Jama'ah, beware of separation, for indeed Ash-Shaitan is with one, and he is further away from two. Whoever wants the best place in Paradise, then let him stick to the Jama'ah. Whoever rejoices with his good deeds and grieves over his evil deeds, then that is the  believer among you.'"""
"2234","Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w): 'There was never a Prophet after Nuh but that he warned his people about the Dajjal"
"2235","'Indeed Allah will not gather my Ummah "" - or he said: ""Ummah upon deviation, and Allah's Hand is over the Jama'ah, and whoever deviates, he deviates to the Fire."""
"2236","""O you people! You recite this Ayah: Take care of yourselves! If you follow the guidance no harm shall come to you. I indeed heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) saying: 'When the people see the wrongdoer and they do not take him by the hand, then soon Allah shall envelope you in a punishment from him.'"""
"2237","""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Either you command good and forbid evil, or Allah will soon send upon you a punishment from Him, then you will call upon Him, but He will not respond to you. """
"2238","Qutaybah narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿAbd Allāh — who is Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī al-Ashhalī — from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān (may Allāh be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour shall not come until you kill your leader (imām), fight among yourselves with your swords, and the worst among you inherit your worldly possessions.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan hadīth. We only know it from the narration of ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr."
"2239","'Perhaps there are those among them who are averse to it."" He said: ""They will be resurrected on their intentions."""
"2240","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Bundār, who narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, who narrated from Sufyān, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, who said:**

""The first person to deliver the sermon (*khutbah*) before the prayer was Marwān. A man stood up and said to Marwān, 'You have opposed the Sunnah.' Marwān replied, 'O so-and-so, that which was [previously observed] has been abandoned.'""

**Abū Saʿīd (may Allāh be pleased with him) said:** ""As for this man, he has fulfilled what was incumbent upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) say:

**'Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand; and if he is not able to do so, then with his tongue; and if he is not able to do so, then with his heart — and that is the weakest of faith.'**""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith.""

---

*This hadith is recorded in Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim and is among the most significant narrations concerning the obligation of enjoining good and forbidding evil (al-amr bi-l-maʿrūf wa-l-nahy ʿan al-munkar), establishing a three-tiered hierarchy of rectifying wrongdoing according to one's capacity.*"
"2241","""The parable of the one who upholds Allah's laws and the one who breaches them, is that of a people who drew lots on a ship at sea. Some of them got the upper part, and some of them the lower part. Those on the lower part ascended to get water, spilling it upon those upper part. So those in the upper part say: 'We will not leave you to come up here and bother us.' Then those on the lower part say: 'We should make a hole in the lower part, so we can get water.' If they take them by the hand and stop them, then they will save all of them, and if they leave them, they will all drown.""'"
"2242","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Dajjal will come to Al-Madinah to find the angels have surrounded it. Neither the plague nor the Dajjal will enter it"
"2243","""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) performed Salat, making it long. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! You have performed Salat (in a manner) which you do not ordinarily perform it.' He said: 'Yes, It was a prayer of hope and fear. In it I asked Allah for three things. He granted me two, and withheld one from me. I asked him that my Ummah not be destroyed by drought. He granted that. I asked him that they not be overcome by enemies from other then them. He granted that. And I asked him that some of them not suffer from the harm of others, and He withheld that.""'"
"2244","""Indeed Allah gathered the earth for me so that I saw its east and its west. And surely my Ummah's authority shall reach over all that was shown to me of it. And I have been granted the two treasures; the red and the white. I asked my Lord that my Ummah is not to be destroyed by a universal drought, and that He does not overcome them by enemies outside of them, reaching to their heart of power. My Lord said: 'O Muhammad! When I issue a decree it is not reversed. I have granted for your Ummah that they shall not be destroyed by universal drought. And that they not be overcome by enemies outside of themselves reaching to their heart of power- even if they gather against them from all the regions.""' 	Or he said: ""Among the regions. But some of them will destroy others, and some will capture others.""'"
"2245","""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Who is the best of people during it?' He said: 'A man among his livestock, who pays what is due on them, and worships his Lord. And a man clutching a head of his horse, terrified of his enemy, and they terrified oh him.""'"
"2246","""There shall be a Fitnah of extermination of the 'Arabs. Its fighters are in the Fire. During it, the tongue is stronger then the sword."""
"2247","""The Messenger of Allah {s.a.w} narrated two narrations to us, one of which I have seen {happening} and I am waiting for the other. He narrated that (in the beginning) trust was preserved in the roots of the hearts of men, then the Qur'an was revealed, and they learned it from the Qur'an, and then they learned it from the Sunnah. Then he narrated to us about the disappearance of trust, saying, 'A man will go to sleep whereupon trust will be taken away from his heart, and only its trace will remain, like speckles. He then will sleep, whereupon the remainder of the trust will also be taken away and trace will remain like a blister, like an ember that you roll on your feet, it causes pain and you see it swollen while it contains nothing.' Then he took a pebble and rolled it over his leg. He said: 'So there will come a day when people will deal in business with each other, but there will hardly be any trustworthy persons among them, such that it would be said that in such and such a tribe, there is such and such person, who is honest, and until a man will be admired for his strength, intelligence, and good manners, although indeed he will not have faith equal to a mustard seed in his heart.""' He (Hudhaifah) added:  ""There came upon me a time when I did not mind dealing with anyone of you, for if he was a Muslim, his religion would prevent him from cheating me, and if was a Jew or a Christian, his Muslim ruler would prevent him from cheating me; but today I cannot deal except with so-and-so and so-and-so."""
"2248","""O Messenger of Allah! Make a Dhat Anwat for us as they have a Dhat Anwat.' The Prophet (s.a.w) said: ""Subhan Allah! This is like what Musa's people said: Make for us a god like their gods. By the One in Whose is my soul! You shall follow the way of those who were before you."""
"2249","Narrated Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ, who narrated from his father, from al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl, from Abū Naḍrah al-ʿAbdī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour shall not be established until wild beasts speak to humans, until the tip of a man’s whip and the strap of his sandal speak to him, and until his thigh informs him of what his family has done after him.""

Abū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: There are narrations on this authority from Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه. This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith; we do not know it except through the narration of al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl. Al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl is trustworthy (*thiqah*) and reliable (*maʾmūn*) among the scholars of hadith, and he was declared trustworthy by Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī."
"2250","Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from al-Aʿmash, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said:

""The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Bear witness (to this).'""

Abū ʿĪsā said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Ibn Masʿūd, Anas, and Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim. This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."
"2251","# Hadith of the Ten Signs of the Hour

## Text

Narrated by Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd (may Allāh be pleased with him):

He said: ""The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) appeared upon us from a chamber while we were discussing the Hour (as-Sāʿah). The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said:

**'The Hour shall not commence until you witness ten signs: the rising of the sun from its place of setting, the emergence of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj (Gog and Magog), the emergence of the Dābbah (the Beast), three land-swallowings (khusūf): a land-swallowing in the East, a land-swallowing in the West, and a land-swallowing in the Arabian Peninsula, and a fire that emerges from the depths of ʿAden (in Yemen) that drives the people or gathers the people, and it shall pass the night with them wherever they pass the night, and it shall take its midday rest with them wherever they take their midday rest.'**

---

## Additional Narrations

**Chain of Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān → Wakīʿ → Sufyān → Furāt:**

A similar narration, with the addition of **""ad-Dukhān"" (the Smoke)**.

**Chain of Hunnād → Abū al-Aḥwaṣ → Furāt al-Qazzāz:**

A similar narration to that of Wakīʿ from Sufyān.

**Chain of Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān → Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī → Shuʿbah and al-Masʿūdī, both from Furāt al-Qazzāz:**

A similar narration to that of ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān from Sufyān from Furāt, with the addition of **""ad-Dajjāl (the False Christ) or the Smoke.""**

**Chain of Abū Mūsā (Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā) → Abū an-Nuʿmān al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbdillāh al-ʿIjlī → Shuʿbah → Furāt:**

A similar narration to that of Abū Dāwūd from Shuʿbah, with the addition that he said:

**'And the tenth sign is either a wind that casts them into the sea, or the descent of ʿĪsā (Jesus), son of Maryam (ʿalayhimā as-salām).'**

---

## Scholarly Notes

Abū ʿĪsā (at-Tirmidhī, raḥimahullāh) stated: ""And in this chapter (there are also narrations) from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), Umm Salamah (may Allāh be pleased with her), and Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy (may Allāh be pleased with her).""

**Abū ʿĪsā declared this ḥadīth to be: Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ (Good and Authentic).**

---

*This ḥadīth is recorded in the Sunan of at-Tirmidhī and constitutes one of the foundational narrations regarding the Major Signs of the Last Hour, including the emergence of the Dajjāl, the descent of ʿĪsā ibn Maryam (ʿalayhimā as-salām), the emergence of the Dābbah, the release of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj, the rising of the sun from the West, the Smoke (ad-Dukhān), three major land-swallowings, and the fire from Yemen that will drive humanity to their place of gathering (al-Mashʿar).*"
"2252","'The people will not finish attacking this House until it is attacked by an army which, when they are at Al-Baida', or a Baida' in the land, it will swallow from the first of them to the last of them, and the middle of them shall not be saved.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah(s.a.w)! What about those among them who are averse to it?' He said: 'Allah will resurrect them upon what was in their souls(intentions).""'"
"2253","'In the end of this Ummah there will be a collapse, transformation, and Qadhf.""' She said :""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Will they be destroyed while they are righteous among them?' He said: 'Yes, when evil is dominant.""'"
"2254","# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us:** Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from his father, from Abū Dharr (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

""I entered the mosque when the sun had set, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) was sitting. He said: **'O Abū Dharr, do you know where this (the sun) goes?'** I said: **'Allāh and His Messenger know best.'** He said: **'Indeed, it goes and seeks permission to prostrate (in worship), and permission is granted to it. It is as though it is said to it: ""Rise from whence you came,"" and so it rises from its place of setting (i.e., the west).'**

He (the narrator) then recited: **'And that is its resting place'** (Sūrah Yāsīn, 36:38). He said: **'And that was the recitation of 'Abdullāh ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him).'**

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **'In this chapter (there are narrations) from Ṣafwān ibn 'Assāl, Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd, Anas, and Abū Mūsā (may Allāh be pleased with them all).'**

**And this is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.**

---

*Note: This hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and is also found in Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī and Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim. It describes the sun's prostration beneath the Throne ('Arsh) of Allāh, as referenced in the Qur'ānic verse: ""And the sun runs [on course] toward its stopping point. That is the determination of the Exalted in Might, the Knowing"" (Sūrah Yāsīn, 36:38).*"
"2255","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Zainab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her):**

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) awoke from sleep with his face flushed red, and he was saying: *""Lā ilāha illallāh""* (There is no god but Allah), repeating it three times. He then said: **""Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn close! Today, a breach has been made in the barrier of Ya'jūj and Ma'jūj (Gog and Magog) like this""** — and he made a circle by joining his thumb and index finger, forming a ring of ten.

Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I asked, **""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we be destroyed even though there are righteous people among us?""** He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: **""Yes, when wickedness (al-khabath) becomes abundant.""**

---

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhī, may Allah have mercy on him) said:** This is a *hasan sahīh* (good and authentic) hadith. And Sufyān (ibn 'Uyaynah) narrated this hadith with excellence (*jawwada*).

Al-Humaydī, 'Alī ibn al-Madīnī, and other Huffāz (master hadith scholars) narrated from Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah similarly to this.

Al-Humaydī said: Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah said: **""I preserved from al-Zuhrī in this hadith the names of four women: Zainab bint Abī Salamah, from Habībah — and both were the stepdaughters of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — from Umm Habībah, from Zainab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).""**

Ma'mar and others narrated this hadith from al-Zuhrī but did not mention Habībah in the chain. Some of the companions of Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated this hadith from Ibn 'Uyaynah and did not mention Umm Habībah in it."
"2256","Abū Kurayb, Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""There will emerge at the end of time a people who are young in age and foolish in understanding. They will recite the Qurʾān, but it will not pass beyond their throats. They will speak the words of the best of creation, yet they will exit from the religion as an arrow exits the game animal.""

Abū ʿĪsā said: In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿAlī, Abū Saʿīd, and Abū Dharr. This hadith is ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ.

It has been narrated in other hadiths from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, where he described these people who recite the Qurʾān but it does not pass beyond their throats, and who exit from the religion as an arrow exits the game animal — they are the Khawārij, the Ḥarūriyyah, and others among the Khawārij."
"2257","""A man from Ansar said, 'O Messenger of Allah! You appointed so-and-so and did not appoint me. So, the Prophet(s.a.w) said, 'After me you will see preferential treatment, so be patient till you meet me at Al-Hawd.""'"
"2258","Abu Wa'il narrated from Hudhaifah that 'Umar said:""Which of you remembers what the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said about the Fitnah?"" So Hudhaifah said: ""I do."" Hudhaifah said: ""A man's Fitnah is in his family"
"2259","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in the Asr prayer one day while it was still daytime, then he stood up to deliver a sermon, and he did not leave anything that would happen up until the establishment of the Hour without informing us of it. Whoever memorized it, memorized it, and whoever forgot it, forgot it. Among the things he said was: 'Indeed this world is sweet and green (attractive), and Allah is going to place you as successors in it, then He will see how you act. So beware of this world and beware of women.' And among what he said was: 'Indeed, let not the awe of people prevent any man from speaking the truth when he knows it.'"" He (the narrator) said: ""Abu Sa'eed wept and said: 'By Allah, we have seen things and felt awed.'"" And among what he said was: ""Indeed a banner will be raised for every treacherous person on the Day of Judgement according to the extent of his treachery, and there is no treachery greater than that of a leader of the common people, whose banner will be planted at his rear."" And among what we memorized that day was: ""Indeed the children of Adam were created in various different levels: among them is one who is born a believer, lives as a believer, and dies a believer; among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives as a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever; among them is one who is born a believer, lives as a believer, and dies a disbeliever; and among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives as a disbeliever, and dies a believer. Indeed, among them is one who is slow to anger and quick to calm down, and among them is one who is quick to anger and quick to calm down - so that balances out that. Indeed, among them is one who is quick to anger and slow to calm down. Indeed, the best of them is the one who is slow to anger and quick to calm down, and indeed the worst of them is the one who is quick to anger and slow to calm down. Indeed, among them is one who repays well and asks well (of his due), and among them is one who repays badly but asks well, and among them is one who repays well but asks badly - so that balances out that. Indeed, among them is one who repays badly and asks badly. Indeed, the best of them is the one who repays well and asks well, and indeed the worst of them is the one who repays badly and asks badly. Indeed, anger is like a burning coal in the heart of the son of Adam. Have you not seen the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his veins? So whoever feels something of that, let him cling to the ground."" He (the narrator) said: ""We began looking towards the sun to see how much of it remained."" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed, what has passed of this world compared to what remains of it is just like what has passed of this day of yours compared to what remains of it.""

[Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from Hudhaifah, Abu Maryam, Abu Zaid bin Akhtab, and Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah, and it is mentioned that the Prophet (ﷺ) informed them of what would happen up until the establishment of the Hour. This Hadith is Hasan."
"2260","""When the inhabitants of Ash-Sham become corrupt, then there is no good in it for you. There will never cease to be a group in my Ummah who will be helped(by Allah), they will not be harmed by those who forsake them until the Hour is established."" Muhammad bin Isma'il said: ""Ali bin Al-Madini said: 'They are the people of Hadith.""'"
"2261","Narrated by Abu Hafs, Amr ibn Ali, who narrated from Yahya ibn Said, who narrated from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, who narrated from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revert to disbelief after me by striking the necks of one another."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Jarir, Ibn Umar, Kurz ibn Alqamah, Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', and al-Sunabihi. This Hadith is Hasan Sahih."
"2262","During the Fitnah(in the time) of 'Uthman bin 'Affan, Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas said: ""I testify that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'There will be a Fitnah during which the sitting person is better than the standing(person) is better than the walking, and the walking(person) is better than the running.""' He said: ""What do you see(I should do) if he entered upon me in my homeand extended hos hand to kill me? He said: 'Be as Adam's son.""'"
"2263","""Rush to do good deeds. A Fitnah will occur that is like a portion of the dark night, morning will come upon a man as a believer, who will be a disbeliever in the evening, and evening will come upon a believer, who will be a disbeliever in the morning. One of them will sell his religion for goods of the world."""
"2264","""One night the Prophet (ﷺ) awoke and said, 'Subhan Allah! How many Fitan (trials and afflictions) have descended tonight. And how many treasures have been disclosed? Who will awaken the women sleeping in these dwellings? O! How many are clothed in this world, yet naked in the Hereafter.'"""
"2265","""Before the Hour there shall be Fitan like a portion of the dark night. Morning will come upon a man as a believer, who will be a disbeliever in the evening, and evening will come upon a believer, who will be a disbeliever in the morning, people will sell their religion for goods of the world."""
"2266","""  Morning will come upon a man as a believer, who will be a disbeliever in the evening, and evening will come upon a believer, who will be a disbeliever in the morning"" - he said: ""Morning would come while his brother's blood, honor and wealth was sacred, and when evening would come, he would consider it lawful for him. And evening would come while his brother's blood, honor and wealth was sacred, and when morning would come, he would  consider it lawful for him."""
"2267","""I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) while a man was asking him: 'What do you see that we should do if there are leaders over us who deny our rights, while they seek their rights?' So the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'Listen and obey, for only they are responsible for their burdens, and only you are responsible for your burdens.""'"
"2268","""Indeed after you there will be days in which knowledge shall be raised up and Al-Harj shall abound."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah(s.a.w)! What is Al-Harj?"" He said: ""Killing."""
"2269","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Black standards will come from Khurasan"
"2270","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""When time draws near"
"2271","""Ali bin Abi Talib came to my father to call him to go out(to fight) with him. My father said to him: 'Indeed my beloved, the son of your paternal uncle, made a covenant with me, that when the people differ, to take a sword of wood. So I have resigned it, if you wish I will take it out with you.' She said: 'So he left him.""'"
"2272","Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'Indeed Messenger-ship and Prophethood have been terminated"
"2273","""I shall narrate a Hadith to you that I heard from the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w), which none after me shall narrate that he heard it from the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w).""  ""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'Indeed, among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge shall be raised up, ignorance shall be rampant, Zina shall abound, Khamr shall be drunk, women shall increase and men shall decrease such that fifty women will be supported by one man."""
"2274","""We entered upon Anas bin Malik. We complained to him about what we were experiencing from Al-Hajjaj. So he said: 'There will not be a year, except that the one that is after it will be more evil than it, until you meet your Lord. I heard this from your Prophet(s.a.w).""'"
"2275","Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour shall not come until it is no longer said upon the earth: 'Allah, Allah.'""

Abu Isa (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a Hasan (good) Hadith.

It was also narrated by Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Humaid, from Anas, with a similar narration, but he did not raise it (i.e., he did not attribute it to the Prophet). And this (the Mawquf version) is more authentic than the first Hadith (the Marfu' version)."
"2276",""" The earth will throw out pieces of its liver(in sides): liver; gold and silver will come out like columns."" He said: ""A thief will come and say: 'For this my hands were amputated?' A murderer will come and say: 'For this I killed?' One who severed ties of kinship will come and say: 'For this I severed the ties of kinship?' Then they will leave it without taking anything from it.""'"
"2277","Abu Qatadah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Dreams are from Allah and Hulum are from Shaitan. So when one of you sees something that bothers him"
"2278","""When my Ummah does fifteen things, the afflictions will occur in it."" It was said: ""What are they O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""When Al-Maghnam (the spoils of war) are distributed (preferentially), trust is usurped, Zakah is a fine, a man obeys his wife and disobeys his mother, he is kind to his friend and abandons his father, voices are raised in the Masajid, the leader of the people is the most despicable among them, the most honored man is the one whose evil the people are afraid of, intoxicants are drunk, silk is worn (by males), there is a fascination for singing slave-girls and music, and the end of this Ummah curses its beginning. When that occurs, anticipate a red wind, collapsing of the earth, and transformation."""
"2279","""When Al-Fai' is distributed(preferentially), trust is a spoil of war, Zakat is a fine, knowledge is sought for other than the(sake of the) religion, a man obeys his wife and disobeys his mother, he is close to his friend and far from his father, voices are raised in the Masajid, tribes are led by their wicked, the leader of the people is the most despicable among them, the most honored man is the one whose evil the people are afraid of, singing slave-girls and music spread, intoxicants are drunk, and the end of this Ummah curses its beginning- then anticipate a red wind, earthquake, collapsing of the earth, transformation, Qadhf, and the signs follow in succession like gems of a necklace whose string is cut and so they fall in succession."""
"2280","""In this Ummah there shall be collapsing of the earth, transformation and Qadhf."" A man among the Muslims said: ""O Messenger of Allah! When is that?"" He said: ""When singing slave-girls, music, and drinking intoxicants spread."""
"2281","""I was sent in advance of the Hour, so that I precede it like this precedes this."" (Indicating) with his index and middle fingers."
"2282","(another chain) from Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami who narrated from 'Ali from the Prophet with similar narrations. [He said:This narration is Hasan.] There are narration on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas"
"2283","""The Hour shall not be established until you fight a people whose sandals are made out of hair, and the Hour shall not be established until you fight a people whose faces will look like shields coated with leather."""
"2284","""When Kisra is ruined, there will be no Kisra after him, and when Caesar is ruined, there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You shall spend their treasures in Allah's cause."""
"2285","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated from some of the companions of the Prophet (s.a.w) that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""While I was sleeping I saw people presented before me"
"2286","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated from Abu Sa'eed al-Khudri that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:similar in meaning (to no)"
"2287","Abu Bakrah narrated:""One day the Prophet (s.a.w) said: ""'Who among you had a dream?' A man said: ""I did. I saw as if a scale had descended from the Heavens in which you and Abu Bakr were weighed So you outweighed Abu Bakr. Abu Bkar and 'Umar were weighed"
"2288","Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) was asked about Waraqah. Khadijah said to him: 'He believed in you"
"2289","""The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them. Then, after them a people will come who increase in fatness, loving fatness, giving testimony before they are asked for it."""
"2290","""The best of my Ummah is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them."" He(`Imran) said: I do not know if he mentioned the third or not. ""Then there shall appear people who testify while their testimony was not sought, who are treacherous, not trusted, and fatness shall spread among them."""
"2291","'There will be twelve Amir after me.""' He said: ""Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me, who said that he(s.a.w) had said: 'All of them are from Quraish.""'"
"2292","Ibn 'abbas narrated fro Abu Hurairah that the Messengr of Allah (s.a.w) said:""I had a dream while sleeping as if there were two gold bracelets in my hands which bothered me very much. So it was reveled to me to blow them off. I blew them off and they flew away. I interpreted thwm to be two liars who would appear after me. One of them caled Masalamah of Yamamah"
"2293","""It was said to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: 'Perhaps you should endorse your successor.' He said: 'If I appoint a successor, then indeed Abu Bakr appointed a successor. And if I do not appoint a successor, the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) did not appoint a successor.""'"
"2294","""Safinah narrated to me, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: ""Al-Khilafah will be in my Ummah for thirty years, then there will be monarchy after that.""' Then Safinah said to me: 'Count the Khilafah of Abu Bakr,' then he said: 'Count the Khilafah of 'Umar and the Khilafah of 'Uthman.' Then he said to me: 'Count the Khilafah of 'Ali.""' He said: ""So we found that they add up to thirty years."" Sa'eed said: ""I said to him: 'Banu Umaiyyah claim that the Khilafah is among them.' He said: 'Banu Az-Zarqa' lie, rather they are a monarchy, among the worst of monarchies.""'"
"2295",""" There were some people from(the tribe of) Rabiah with 'Amr bin Al-'As, so a man from(the tribe of) Bakr bin Wa'il said: ""Either the Quraish will stop, or Allah will place this matter among the masses of the Arabs other than them.' So 'Amr bin Al-'As said: 'You have lied, I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying: ""The Quraish are the leaders of the people, in the good and the bad, until the Day of Judgement."""
"2296","Muhammad ibn Bashshar al-Abdiyy narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafiyy narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The night and the day shall not pass until a man from the freedmen (mawali) shall rule, whose name shall be Jahjah."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan gharib hadith."
"2297","""I only fear for my Ummah from the misguiding A'immah."" He said that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: ""There will never cease to be a group from my Ummah manifest upon the truth, they will not be harmed by those who forsake them until Allah's Decree comes."""
"2298","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:The testimony of a treacherous man is not acceptable nor a treacherous woman nor a man lashed for the Hadd nor a woman lashed nor one possessing malice of enmity nor a rehearsed witness nor the Qani of (one contracted by)the family on their behalf nor the one associating himself to other than his Wala or to other than his relatives"
